Yes, you can use the bundled Chulapa font without external loading. To use it on headings, you must first set the font family under `chulapa-skin.vars`. Setting the family is required because ligature CSS alone does not select the font.

1. In your configuration, set `headings-font-family: "chulapa, sans-serif"` under `chulapa-skin.vars`.
2. To enable ligatures, add the following to your `assets/css/custom.scss` (ensuring you preserve empty YAML front matter):

```scss
---
---
h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 {
  font-feature-settings: "liga", "dlig";
  text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
}
```

Alternatively, you can apply the font inline using `<span class="chulapa">Chulapa</span>` or `{: .chulapa}` after a Markdown paragraph.

Source: [Bundled font](https://dieghernan.github.io/chulapa/docs/53-chulapa-font)
